{"id": "EUVD-2026-81949", "enisaUuid": "41dc4a71-2449-344f-b1fb-7c99df5cc966", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: RFCOMM: Validate MTU in rfcomm_apply_pn() to prevent infinite loop\n\nrfcomm_apply_pn() accepts the MTU value from a remote PN (Parameter\nNegotiation) frame without checking for zero. When the remote peer\nsends an MTU of zero, d->mtu is set to 0. This causes the sendmsg\npath to enter an infinite loop when fragmenting data, as each fragment\nhas size == min_t(size_t, len, 0) == 0, so the remaining length never\ndecreases. The infinite allocation of zero-length skbs exhausts all\nsystem memory.\n\nFix by clamping d->mtu to RFCOMM_DEFAULT_MTU when the negotiated\nvalue is zero, consistent with the initial value assigned in\nrfcomm_dlc_alloc().", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:06:03", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:57:45", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e7c0aa45ae6c5a338661b23812bfcdef50bf3e96", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cbc2962da99b6b89345267d3aa74b4b573340548", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9b2e5f1928c99224345a9ed8c5dae5fc74964d6d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fc4851ff8dfb505e9a19efcc286712132bbd178d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f561e44261344adadf9d6a6dff31e3af9776d5c6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aeee917a4878af95f0c63e18c5f22eaf6299c7b8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3988cbb1be501dbff909a2ee024670e3c955a66d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/44c98fd082eafd49d55a8a4077ff488175b2fe24"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90088", "GHSA-j6jv-mcf5-3925"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "01ae4c05-8aa0-343a-baa8-a273eb3a9eb1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "0d2d8e19-606d-3a04-bea8-0da5770ab777", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <e7c0aa45ae6c5a338661b23812bfc